    "turns": 33,
    "tool_calls": 33,
    "summary": "Fixed the wfmt package to satisfy all acceptance criteria:\n\n1. **varint.py**: Fixed `decode_uvarint` to properly handle multi-byte LEB128 (was broken, only reading 1 byte).\n\n2. **header.py**: Changed count encoding from big-endian to little-endian (`<I`) to match the actual sample format.\n\n3. **crc.py**: Added final XOR (`^ 0xFFFFFFFF`) to `compute_crc` to produce standard CRC-32 (ISO 3309), matching the samples. Updated `unpack_crc` to raise WFormatError.\n\n4. **codec.py**: Added 4-byte alignment padding to `encode_record` and padding-skipping to `decode_record`. Added CRC verification to `unpack`. All errors use WFormatError with proper kinds.\n\n5. **stream.py**: Rewrote `iter_records` to be truly streaming using a `_StreamReader` class that reads in fixed CHUNK_SIZE blocks, never calling `read()` without arguments. Handles varint parsing, alignment, and post-record CRC verification.\n\nKey format discoveries from reverse-engineering the samples:\n- Header: magic(4B) + version(1B) + count",
    "changed_workspace": true
  },
